From edf915462e0d567d963b3f7b25f5e2f3f7b82e4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KONKR Pocket FIT Elite port <unknown-email@domain.tld>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:06:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 093/165] ASoC: wcd939x: add HPH PCM (HiFi) mode

In HPH PCM mode the headphone stream arrives as PCM samples on the
HIFI_PCM SoundWire port and the codec runs its own interpolator, DC
droop filter and compander instead of the PDM receive path. Selected
with the "HPH PCM Switch" control.

From the SM8750 handheld series carried by ROCKNIX and Armbian
(patch/kernel/archive/sm8750-7.2/0073); the SoundWire port controls
rebased onto the per-channel mask code.
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c | 319 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 292 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
index 1ee6763f7244..0c5c221b444f 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
@@ -209,6 +209,7 @@ struct wcd939x_priv {
 	int ear_pdm_wd_int;
